1. Identify all existing Playwright E2E tests located in the `tests/e2e/` directory.2. For each of the following Phase 2 features, either update existing tests or create new, comprehensive tests:
    - New decline flow UI
    - First-conquest border/coastal restriction and highlighting
    - Corrected conquest cost calculation and tooltip
    - Reinforcement die flow reordering
    - Left/right-click redeployment model
    - Interaction/pan mode toggle
    - Combo HUD browse mode
    - Race/power text labels and tooltips
    - Player box ability tooltips
    - Redrawn region polygons
3. Ensure all new and updated tests adhere to Playwright best practices, including clear selectors, robust assertions, and maintainability. Utilize page object models where appropriate to abstract page interactions.
4. Example pseudo-code for updating a test for the new decline flow UI:
```javascript
// tests/e2e/declineFlow.spec.js
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('should correctly display and interact with the new decline flow UI', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/game-setup'); // Navigate to a state where decline flow can be triggered
  // Simulate game actions to reach a state where the decline flow is presented
  // For example, if a specific game event triggers it:
  await page.locator('#start-game-button').click();
  await page.waitForSelector('.decline-flow-modal');

  // Assert visibility and content of the decline flow modal
  await expect(page.locator('.decline-flow-modal')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('.decline-flow-modal h2')).toHaveText('Decline Offer');
  await expect(page.locator('.decline-flow-option-button')).toHaveCount(2); // Assuming two options

  // Test interaction, e.g., clicking an option
  await page.locator('.decline-flow-option-button').first().click();
  await expect(page.locator('.decline-flow-modal')).not.toBeVisible(); // Modal should close
  // Further assertions on game state change after decline
});
```
